# Random modules, whose predicates and functions have random types and
# clauses that fit them, some declared and some inferred, a few with a
# mutation that makes them ill-typed: merkc's type checking and inference
# agree with mmc's (see utils/type-oracle/compare-types.py). The seed is
# fixed, so the modules are too; to search further, run
# generate-random-programs.py with other seeds.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-random-programs.py --seed 2 --count 60 %t
# RUN: %compare-types --allow-errors %t/*.m
